        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## DF drive\n\nFive lanes on one clock, which is a KrakenSDR or equivalent. A single dongle cannot run this: the lanes have to share a clock for the phases to mean anything.\n\n**Array** is the five antennas as one instrument. Mount element 1 facing forward and set the geometry to match your actual ring.\n\n**Direction finder** turns the array into bearings. Its wire to **Triangulation** is what crosses successive bearings into a position as you move, so a drive narrows the fix that a single bearing cannot.\n\n**GPS position** feeds the array its place and heading, and the fix its vehicle. Pick a paired phone here for both, and it gets directions to the fix.\n\n**Signal survey** maps raw signal strength along the same drive, which is the sanity check on a fix the bearings disagree about.\n\nTuned to 433.920 MHz."
          },
          "position": { "x": 0.0, "y": 900.0 }
        }
